+
+## SMS verification during sign-up
+
+The sign-up form collects account details and an international phone number, sends
+an SMS, and creates the account only after the server validates the six-digit code
+with Twilio Verify. Set the server environment variables listed in `.env.example`;
+missing credentials produce an unavailable message rather than simulated success.
+The Node deployment reads these variables at runtime from `process.env`.
+
+Create a Twilio Verify Service with SMS enabled and a **six-digit** token length.
+Configure an approved domain-bound template as the service default, or supply its
+SID in `TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID`. The template must end with the following line,
+using the actual hostname serving the sign-up page (without a scheme or path):
+
+```text
+@your-hostname #{{code}}
+```
+
+See [Twilio's domain-bound SMS setup](https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/developers/tutorials/product/domain-bound-sms-otps-verify).
+On HTTPS, supported browsers can extract the code with WebOTP after user consent.
+The input also uses `autocomplete="one-time-code"` for platform autofill; typing
+and pasting remain available when extraction is unavailable or declined.
+
+The form provides a 30-second resend delay. Configure the Verify Service's fraud
+protection, geographic permissions, and provider-side rate limits for production;
+the UI delay is not a security boundary. Provider throttling is surfaced in the
+form. No credentials, passwords, or verification codes are persisted in browser
+storage. A failed registration after approval requires a fresh SMS verification,
+since the approved code has already been consumed.
+
+Account creation still uses the existing external registration service, forwarding
+`username`, `password`, and the verified `phone`. This repository cannot enforce
+verification on clients calling that external service directly; enforcing this as
+an account-wide policy requires the registration service to accept requests only
+from this trusted server and persist the verified number.
